		<p> Using only the ring axioms, complete the tables.
          Explain how each entry you add can be determined from the ring axioms
          and the entries already completed.
          (Hints: Some important ring axioms are addition being commutative, and
          the distributive property.
          Recall Weekly Practice from Module 1 #3.
          Also, you can use Proof Portfolio Problem 6a, which is true in rings
          (not just fields).
          Note 5b is <em>not</em> true for all rings.)</p>
          <!-- Double-check that I mean PP6a here. It originally said 5a -->
		</statement>
		
		</exercise>
		
		
		<exercise number="4">
		<statement><p> For which <m>n</m> is <m>\mathbb{Z}_{n}</m> an integral domain?
          A field?
		</p></statement>
		
